  "id": "DrugBank_DB00635 - MONDO_11292",
  "verbalization": "Prednisone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Dermatitis, Atopic through a mechanism involving glucocorticoid receptor activation. The evidence suggests that Prednisone, through its indication on Hydrocortisone Acetate and Dexamethasone, ultimately leads to the manifestation of Dermatitis, Atopic. This is supported by the shared indication of Dermatitis, Atopic in multiple pathways, indicating a potential role in inflammatory or immune-related conditions. The presence of multiple indirect pathways linking Prednisone to Dermatitis, Atopic highlights a possible dependency on glucocorticoid receptor signaling, which is a well-established mechanism in the treatment of inflammatory diseases. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of glucocorticoids in modulating immune responses, suggesting that Prednisone may exert its therapeutic effects through this mechanism.",
